ds, `content-hash`, `segment-key`,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:42:   every handle and descriptor for one stream.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:43:4. A **portable descriptor** is reachability data used to attach to an existing\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:48:Creation is not attachment. A descriptor is not a creation specification or an\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:58:| `attach!`    | portable descriptor    | handle outcome     |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:59:| `descriptor` | handle                 | descriptor outcome |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:91:descriptor's properties, the result keyword namespace, the anchor set — it is\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:104:  operation returns such a map — including projections like `descriptor` and\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:204:  new logical stream. `descriptor` on that handle returns `{ok}` with both\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:205:  `:dao.stream/descriptor`, the transport-specific reachability value, and\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:207:  The descriptor carries the same identity internally; the sibling projection\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:208:  and its value inside `:dao.stream/descriptor` must be structurally equal.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:209:  Both projections are total and outlive any attachment, so `descriptor` has\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:211:- `attach!` consumes a portable descriptor and returns a handle on an\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:212:  attachment to the **same** logical stream the descriptor names. Attaching\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:214:- A creation specification says how to build a stream. A descriptor only\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:226:survive encoding, and any\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:230:transport can carry is transport-owned: handing an encoding transport a\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:232:`attach!` therefore consumes only descriptors, and\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:236:registry maps descriptors to live handles, so a descriptor arriving\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:237:somewhere with nothing behind it — a ring buffer's descriptor on any other\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:241:### Envelopes\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:253:The **portable descriptor** is inspired by CORBA's interoperable object\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:260:  `:dao.stream/identity` key. Different descriptors may reach\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:263:  descriptor attaches to the same stream every time.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:267:  `:dao.stream/invalid-descriptor`.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:282:  a descriptor is a name, and a host that can reach what it names attaches.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:290:For the time being, the operative guarantee is the round trip: `descriptor`\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:291:on a live handle returns `:dao.stream/ok` with `:dao.stream/descriptor`,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:293:`:dao.stream/identity`, equal through every handle and descriptor for the\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:320:| `:dao.stream/invalid-descriptor` | The descriptor is malformed.                                                        | —                    |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:321:| `:dao.stream/not-found`          | The descriptor names no stream here, or no transport matches its type.              | —                    |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:349:When a creation specification or portable descriptor arrives dynamically —\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:388:Retention and Gaps sections govern handles with a reader surface only.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:390:`descriptor` belongs to no surface: every handle answers it with both\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:503:  declared retention (see *Retention and Gaps*), never from an anchor.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:521:  descriptor envelope.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:522:- A cursor carries the logical-stream identity, not a reachability descriptor.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:524:  descriptors for the same logical stream accept the same cursor.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:561:| `:dao.stream/full`            | The transport does not accept the value; nothing was appended. Whether this is transient or permanent is the transport's declared nature (see Retention and Gaps). | —             |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:595:stream persists, its descriptor remains valid, and `attach!` may rejoin\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:602:closes, the handle's `append!` answers `closed`; `descriptor` still answers\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:650:## Retention and Gaps\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:759:## Explicitly Absent\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
